ble poll is 57 days old; polling uncertainty inflated.", "Incumbent Wes Moore (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Maryland's governor's race is a rematch between incumbent Democrat Wes Moore and Republican Dan Cox, who ran against Moore in 2022. Moore enters with the advantages of incumbency in a state that leans Democratic by about fifteen points, and he has raised roughly $15.5 million to Cox's $242,000. Every major race rater calls the contest Safe or Solid Democratic, and prediction markets put Moore's win chances in the mid-to-high 90s.\n\nThe only recent poll, from early August, showed Moore ahead 58-31 among likely voters; earlier surveys from 2025 and January 2026 showed leads of roughly twenty points. Cox has campaigned on electricity costs and data center policy, and the two are set to debate in October, but he has limited resources to change the race's fundamentals. The state's partisan balance and Moore's financial dominance make an upset unlikely.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.996, "margin": 19.52}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9967, "margin": 19.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.998, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9939, "margin": 20.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9968, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9958, "margin": 21.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9956, "margin": 19.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9959, "margin": 19.5}]}